+## Bounded retrieval proposal, 2026-11-07
+
+The implemented search still reads complete channels and observes all candidates.
+The user clarified: an omitted search limit defaults to 100; an explicit positive
+limit uses min(limit, 100). Database retrieval must use that effective bound.
+Both FTS and nearest-vector matching, ordering and candidate limiting must run
+in SQLite. Rust receives only selected candidate IDs and ranking metadata;
+loading complete channels and truncating in process memory is disallowed by the
+new design. This bounds application result materialization, not the SQLite
+engine's internal memory or exact vector scanning work.
+Proposed application: at most this many knowledge hits per channel, union at most
+twice that number, then fresh checks, filters and reciprocal-rank fusion; return
+at most the effective limit. For limit 5, each channel returns at most 5, not 100.
+This changes full-corpus filtered ranking and errors outside the candidate pool;
+selective filters can leave fewer results. Shared vector hashes must not evade
+the joined knowledge-hit cap. Product code and timings are still unchanged.
+The previous 65.83-second measurement used final limit 5.
+
